    "description": "The perimeters of the Alpine Convention in Switzerland. The Alpine Convention is an international treaty between the eight Alpine countries: Germany, France, Italy, Liechtenstein, Monaco, Austria, Switzerland and Slovenia, plus the European Union. The aim of the treaty is to protect the Alps by means of cross-sectoral, integrated and sustainable policies.",
